# Code Quality

## Style

- Prefer simple, robust JavaScript — no build step for runtime code
- async/await for asynchronous operations
- JSDoc on public methods where helpful
- Use `this.log.*` in adapter code — never `console.log` in production adapter code
- Tabs, **single quotes** (match `prettier.config.mjs`)
- ESLint via `@iobroker/eslint-config` — run `npm run lint` after every change and before any release; **0 errors required** (fix with `npx eslint -c eslint.config.mjs . --fix` when Prettier fails)

## Resource cleanup

Clear timers in `onUnload()`; always call `callback()`:

```javascript
onUnload(callback) {
	try {
		if (this.pollTimer) {
			this.clearTimeout(this.pollTimer);
			this.pollTimer = null;
		}
		callback();
	} catch (error) {
		this.log.error(`Error during unload: ${error.message}`);
		callback();
	}
}
```

Prefer a `setTimeout` poll chain over `setInterval` so a slow request cannot overlap the next poll.

## Error handling

- Wrap async/API work in try/catch; log errors, do not crash the adapter
- Network failures: set `info.connection` false; wait for next poll
- Do not retry failed HTTP calls in a tight loop
- **Machine powered off** (`EHOSTUNREACH`, `ECONNREFUSED`, timeout, …): log **once** at **info**, not warn; log **once** at info when reachable again. Do not flood the log every poll cycle.

## HTTP

- **Preferred:** native `node:http` / `node:https`
- **Avoid:** axios, request
- Snapmaker API: `http://host:8080/api/v1/…` with form-urlencoded bodies where Luban does (`connect`, etc.)
- Reasonable timeouts (e.g. 5–10 s) on every request

## Dependencies

- Node.js >= 22
- `@iobroker/adapter-core`; avoid unnecessary dependencies
- Prefer built-in Node modules
